<attribute name="sectionName" nodeId="873117ec"></attribute>
<attribute name="sectionDescription" nodeId="78818f1a">&lt;p&gt;
    Relevant test metrics include, but are not limited to, the following:
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Productivity
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Total number of test scripts
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Number of executed test scripts
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Number of passed test scripts
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Test pass rate
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Target&amp;nbsp;percentage executed
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Percentage passed vs. planned
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Percentage&amp;nbsp;failed vs. planned
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Number of failed test scripts
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Test scripting effective rate
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Number of blocked test scripts
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Number of defects logged
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Number of active defects
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Net active severity 1 and 2 defects
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Number of resolved defects
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Defect retest turnaround effectiveness
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Open vs. closed defect trend
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Defect turnaround rate
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Defect rejection ratio
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Capacity utilization
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    These metrics and others may be readily available if a test management tool is used in the test effort. Otherwise,
    these metrics are collected from participants involved in the test effort. Once available, the information is reviewed
    and data analysis is performed to prepare the metrics and key messages communicated to stakeholders.
&lt;/p&gt;</attribute>
